pub const SAY_HONEST : str = "Every ternary design here is binary-encoded and synthesised onto binary LUTs. That is not ternary hardware, and it says nothing about a native ternary circuit; it says what carrying trits through a binary FPGA costs. No t27 spec is an n-trit multiplier, so there is no ternary multiplier curve.";
